*****************************CIGARETTES (PAST 30 DAYS).
*Q: During the past 30 days, on how many days did you smoke cigarettes? (H3TO7)
*   Asked only of current/regular smokers. Non-smokers skip entire cigarette section.
***check frequencies for zeros.
frequencies variables = H3TO7 H3TO6 H3TO4 H3TO1 /statistics = all.
*answer codes (H3TO7): 0 to 30 = days smoked,
*                       96 = refused,
*                       97 = legitimate skip [never smoked regularly or not smoking in past 30 days],
*                       98 = don't know,
*                       99 = not applicable.
*answer codes (H3TO6): 0 = no (did not smoke in past 30 days),
*                       1 = yes,
*                       97 = legitimate skip [never smoked an entire cigarette].
*answer codes (H3TO1): 0 = never tried cigarettes [skip entire section].

*Creating cigarette days variable (0-30 continuous).
*Non-smokers (never tried, never smoked regularly, or not smoking in past 30) = 0.
*H3TO7 is only asked if H3TO6=1 (smoked in past 30 days).
*Respondents who never tried (H3TO1=0) or smoked regularly but not in past 30 (H3TO6=0) = 0.
if (H3TO1 eq 0) cig30 = 0.
if (H3TO6 eq 0) cig30 = 0.
if (H3TO7 ge 0 and H3TO7 le 30) cig30 = H3TO7.
if (H3TO7 eq 96 or H3TO7 eq 98 or H3TO7 eq 99) cig30 = -99.
recode cig30 (-99 = sysmis).
variable labels cig30
    "Days smoked cigarettes in past 30 days (H3TO7, W3, 0=none, higher=more use)".
value labels cig30
    0 "0 days"
    30 "30 days (every day)".
execute.

*check frequencies of new variable.
frequencies variables = cig30 /statistics = all.
*******************************************************************************

*****************************ALCOHOL USE FREQUENCY PAST 12 MONTHS.
*Q: During the past 12 months, on how many days did you drink alcohol? (H3TO38)
***check frequencies for zeros.
frequencies variables = H3TO38 H3TO37 /statistics = all.
*answer codes (H3TO38): 0 = none (did not drink in past 12 months),
*                        1 = 1 or 2 days in the past 12 months,
*                        2 = once a month or less (3 to 12 times in the past 12 months),
*                        3 = 2 or 3 days a month,
*                        4 = 1 or 2 days a week,
*                        5 = 3 to 5 days a week,
*                        6 = every day or almost every day,
*                        96 = refused,
*                        97 = legitimate skip [never had more than 2-3 drinks since June 1995],
*                        98 = don't know,
*                        99 = not applicable.
*answer codes (H3TO37): 0 = no [skip to Q.50 — never had drink more than 2-3 times since June 1995],
*                        1 = yes.

*Passing through ordinal 0-6 scale; non-drinkers (H3TO37=0) coded 0.
*Higher values = more frequent alcohol use.
if (H3TO37 eq 0) alcfreq = 0.
if (H3TO38 ge 0 and H3TO38 le 6) alcfreq = H3TO38.
if (H3TO38 eq 96 or H3TO38 eq 98 or H3TO38 eq 99) alcfreq = -99.
recode alcfreq (-99 = sysmis).
variable labels alcfreq
    "Alcohol use frequency past 12 months (H3TO38, W3, 0-6 ordinal, higher=more frequent)".
value labels alcfreq
    0 "none"
    1 "1 or 2 days in past 12 months"
    2 "once a month or less (3-12 times)"
    3 "2 or 3 days a month"
    4 "1 or 2 days a week"
    5 "3 to 5 days a week"
    6 "every day or almost every day".
execute.

*check frequencies of new variable.
frequencies variables = alcfreq /statistics = all.
******************************************************************************

*****************************BINGE DRINKING FREQUENCY PAST 12 MONTHS.
*Q: During the past 12 months, on how many days did you drink five or more drinks in a row? (H3TO40)
***check frequencies for zeros.
frequencies variables = H3TO40 H3TO37 /statistics = all.
*answer codes (H3TO40): 0 = none,
*                        1 = 1 or 2 days in the past 12 months,
*                        2 = once a month or less (3 to 12 times in the past 12 months),
*                        3 = 2 or 3 days a month,
*                        4 = 1 or 2 days a week,
*                        5 = 3 to 5 days a week,
*                        6 = every day or almost every day,
*                        96 = refused,
*                        97 = legitimate skip [never had more than 2-3 drinks since June 1995],
*                        98 = don't know,
*                        99 = not applicable.

*Passing through ordinal 0-6 scale; non-drinkers (H3TO37=0) coded 0.
*Higher values = more frequent binge drinking.
if (H3TO37 eq 0) bingefreq = 0.
if (H3TO40 ge 0 and H3TO40 le 6) bingefreq = H3TO40.
if (H3TO40 eq 96 or H3TO40 eq 98 or H3TO40 eq 99) bingefreq = -99.
recode bingefreq (-99 = sysmis).
variable labels bingefreq
    "Binge drinking frequency past 12 months (H3TO40, W3, 0-6 ordinal, higher=more frequent)".
value labels bingefreq
    0 "none"
    1 "1 or 2 days in past 12 months"
    2 "once a month or less (3-12 times)"
    3 "2 or 3 days a month"
    4 "1 or 2 days a week"
    5 "3 to 5 days a week"
    6 "every day or almost every day".
execute.

*check frequencies of new variable.
frequencies variables = bingefreq /statistics = all.

*****************************BINGE DRINKING FREQUENCY PAST 12 MONTHS.
*Evans and Watts (2024).
*sum freq and binge freq to get variable with range of 0–12, where higher values denote 
    more alcohol use as measured by frequency of drinking overall and frequency of binge drinking.

compute alc_tot = sum(alcfreq, bingefreq). 
variable labels alc_tot
    "Sum of alcohol frequency and binge frequency past 12 months, 0 -12, higher = more drinking)".
execute.

*check frequencies of new variable.
frequencies variables = alc_tot /statistics = all.
*******************************************************************************

*****************************SUBSTANCE USE — MARIJUANA (PAST 30 DAYS, WAVE 3).
*Q: During the past 30 days, how many times have you used marijuana? (H3TO110)
*   Asked only of past-year users (H3TO109=1). Continuous, times (not days).
*   Winsorizing recommended before z-scoring due to extreme upper values (range up to 500).
***check frequencies for zeros.
frequencies variables = H3TO110 H3TO109 H3TO108 /statistics = all.
*answer codes (H3TO110): 0 = 0 times,
*                         1 to 500 = number of times used,
*                         9996 = refused,
*                         9997 = legitimate skip [did not use marijuana since June 1995 or not in past year],
*                         9998 = don't know,
*                         9999 = not applicable.
*answer codes (H3TO109): 0 = no (not in past year) [skip to Q.111],
*                         1 = yes.
*answer codes (H3TO108): 0 = no (not since June 1995) [skip to Q.111].

*Non-users (H3TO108=0) and past-but-not-recent users (H3TO109=0) = 0.
*Past-year users who reported 0 times in past 30 = 0.
if (H3TO108 eq 0) mj30 = 0.
if (H3TO109 eq 0) mj30 = 0.
if (H3TO110 ge 0 and H3TO110 le 500) mj30 = H3TO110.
if (H3TO110 eq 9996 or H3TO110 eq 9998 or H3TO110 eq 9999) mj30 = -99.
recode mj30 (-99 = sysmis).
variable labels mj30
    "Times used marijuana in past 30 days (H3TO110, W3, 0=none, higher=more use)".
value labels mj30
    0 "0 times".
execute.

*check frequencies and examine distribution before z-scoring — likely right-skewed.
frequencies variables = mj30 /statistics = all.
***very skewed and kurtotic.

examine variables = mj30
    /plot none
    /statistics none
    /percentiles(95) haverage.
*95th = 28.

if (mj30 lt 27) mj30_WSD = mj30.
if (mj30 ge 28) mj30_WSD = 28.
variable labels mj30_WSD
    "Times used marijuana in past 30 days, winsorized at 95th percentile (H3TO110, W3, 0=none, higher=more use)".
execute.

frequencies variables = mj30_WSD  /statistics = all.
*slightly kurtotic, not skewed.

*****************************SUBSTANCE USE — Z-SCORE EACH SUBSTANCE.
*Z-scoring cig30, alc30, and mj30_WSD so each is on the same metric before compositing.
*Following Crane et al. (2021) polysubstance approach.

descriptives variables = cig30 alc_tot mj30_WSD
    /save.
*SPSS will create Zcig30, Zalc30, Zmj30 automatically via /save.
execute.

*Confirm z-scored variables were created.
frequencies variables = Zcig30 Zalc_tot Zmj30_WSD /statistics = all.

*****************************POLYSUBSTANCE USE COMPOSITE SCORE..
*Averaging z-scores of cigarettes, alcohol, and marijuana to create polysubstance composite.
*Higher scores = greater polysubstance use.
compute subuse_w3 = mean(Zcig30, Zalc_tot, Zmj30_WSD).
variable labels subuse_w3
    "Polysubstance use composite, W3 (mean of Zcig30 Zalc_tot Zmj30_WSD, higher=more use)".
execute.

*check frequencies of composite.
frequencies variables = subuse_w3 /statistics = all.

*standardize based on weight filtered dataset.
delete variables  Zsubuse_w3.
    *delete variable if previously standardized with whole sample. 
temporary.
    *temporary can't be used with delete.
select if (GSWGT3_2 ge 0). 
descriptives variables = subuse_w3 / save.
